 "text": "Hi! How are you today? Lots of people learn by doing it, step by step. Would you like beginner lessons, or would you rather start with drawing from memory? Start with simple shapes, like squares and circles, and practice drawing them from different angles. A line drawing is just lines, no colours or shades. A pencil drawing adds colours and shades, and a pen drawing uses pens only. That's a lot of practice. Start with simple things close up, like a spoon on your desk, and build up to faces and landscapes.",
